T}@T{
Explicit rendezvous file printed by the waiting command; required for
\f[CR]auth\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]\-\-help\f[R], \f[CR]\-h\f[R]
T}@T{
Show help for the selected command and exit.
T}
T{
\f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
T}@T{
Print the installed version and exit.
T}
.TE
.PP
\f[CR]init\f[R], \f[CR]cluster add\f[R] and \f[CR]cluster remove\f[R]
are interactive setup commands.
\f[CR]cluster list\f[R] and \f[CR]cluster inspect\f[R] use an existing
session and accept \f[CR]\-\-json\f[R].
\f[CR]resources\f[R] also requires \f[CR]\-\-cluster\f[R] and accepts
repeatable \f[CR]\-\-namespace\f[R] hints.
.SS Creation options
Without a preset, supply name, namespace, owner, image, GPU count and
all three paths.
Supply CPU and memory unless the profile derives them from the GPU
count.
A positive GPU count also requires a GPU type.
With a preset, explicit fields override its saved settings; name and
namespace remain required.
.PP
.TS
